      "Frobenius Method around Regular Singular Point: Assume generalized power series solution y(x) = x^r \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^n = \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty a_n x^{n + r}$ where a_0 \\neq 0.",
      "The Indicial Equation: Lowest power of x yields quadratic equation in r called the Indicial Equation: F(r) = r(r - 1) + p_0 r + q_0 = 0; roots r_1, r_2 determine the form of the two linearly independent solutions.",
      "Frobenius Solution Cases: Case 1: Roots r_1, r_2 distinct and (r_1 - r_2) not an integer \\implies two independent Frobenius series y_1(x) and y_2(x); Case 2: Roots equal (r_1 = r_2) \\implies y_2(x) = y_1(x)\\ln x + \\dots; Case 3: Roots differ by an integer.",
      "Bessel's Differential Equation: x^2 y'' + x y' + (x^2 - n^2) y = 0; solutions are Bessel functions of first kind J_n(x) and second kind (Neumann function) Y_n(x).",
      "Bessel Function Series & Generating Function: J_n(x) = \\sum_{r=0}^\\infty \\frac{(-1)^r}{r! \\Gamma(n + r + 1)} \\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^{n + 2r}; Generating function e^{\\frac{x}{2}(t - 1/t)} = \\sum_{n=-\\infty}^\\infty J_n(x) t^n.",
      "Legendre's Differential Equation: (1 - x^2) y'' - 2x y' + n(n + 1) y = 0; solutions are Legendre polynomials P_n(x) for integer n.",
      "Rodrigues' Formula & Orthogonality of Legendre Polynomials: P_n(x) = \\frac{1}{2^n n!} \\frac{d^n}{dx^n}(x^2 - 1)^n; Orthogonality condition \\int_{-1}^1 P_m(x) P_n(x) \\, dx = \\frac{2}{2n + 1} \\delta_{mn}.",
